SLIDE 19 – KEY SECURITY OBSERVATIONS

Key Observations

• Open ports increase network exposure
• Unnecessary services should be disabled
• Software should remain updated
• Network access should be restricted
• Traffic monitoring helps identify unusual activity
• Security findings should be supported by evidence
• Hardening should be verified through testing


SLIDE 20 – CONCLUSION

Conclusion

The Week 3 practical provided hands-on experience
with network discovery, advanced Nmap scanning,
Wireshark traffic analysis, vulnerability assessment,
and security hardening.

The assessment helped demonstrate how security
weaknesses can be identified, documented,
remediated, and verified using practical tools.

All testing was performed in an authorized
laboratory environment.


